"modules":[],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000078487","entrez_id":["55063"],"uniprot":["Q9H0M4"],"ncbi_summary":"Enables methyl-CpG binding activity and methylated histone binding activity. Predicted to be involved in meiosis I; positive regulation of DNA metabolic process; and spermatogenesis. Predicted to act upstream of or within homologous chromosome pairing at meiosis. Predicted to be located in XY body. Predicted to be active in nucleus. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9H0M4","text":"Dual histone methylation reader specific for PRDM9-catalyzed histone marks (H3K4me3 and H3K36me3) (PubMed:20826339, PubMed:32744506). Facilitates the repair of PRDM9-induced meiotic double-strand breaks (DSBs) (By similarity). Essential for male fertility and spermatogenesis (By similarity). Required for meiosis prophase I progression in male but not in female germ cells (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}